// Added by the Miuix UI rewrite No updates available No apps to show No results Search apps Type at least 2 characters to search across all enabled sources Clear Copied to clipboard Close Filtering Requires opening the browser to download Experimental, requires sign-in Only trusted Aptoide stores Install method How downloaded packages are installed Automatic (root if available) System installer (confirm each time) Root silent install (su) The system installer will always ask for confirmation unless the device is rooted; with root, installs complete silently. XAPK split packages require root. Root status Root granted Root denied Requesting root… Not checked yet, tap to request China-friendly network Use domestic mirrors Rewrite official endpoints to mirrors reachable in mainland China GitHub accelerator Custom accelerator prefix Proxy GitHub release downloads F-Droid repository Custom F-Droid repo URL IzzyOnDroid repository Custom IzzyOnDroid repo URL Direct Network diagnostics Probe every line and pick a reachable one Tap to start probing all lines Probing… Re-run Use fastest GitHub line Use fastest F-Droid mirror No reachable line found This source provides no download link XAPK/APKS split packages require root to install silently Grant "Install unknown apps" permission for this app, then retry
// Empty-state filter hints Note: app-store apps system apps disabled apps ignored apps
// Scanned app count Checked %1$d installed apps
// Grouped update source label %1$d sources
// Update scope + sectioned list Update scope Allow updating system apps System apps (including preinstalled-then-updated ones like Chrome / WebView) will be checked for updates. Sideloading a system app update may fail or cause issues. Include app-store installed apps When off, apps installed by an app store are skipped These options decide which apps are checked for updates. The three icons on the \"Apps\" tab only filter what that list displays. User apps System apps System apps are not being checked. Enable \"Settings → Update scope → Allow updating system apps\" to include them. No system app updates available
// MCP 服务（PC 端 AI Agent 远程控制更新器） MCP Service Enable MCP server Lets a PC AI agent control this updater over the local network: scan, list updates, install, read logs. Port Must be 1024–65535. Changing it restarts the server. Port must be between 1024 and 65535 Allow LAN access Binds to 0.0.0.0 — any device on your network can reach the server. Always rely on the token. Access token Not generated yet Access token Anyone with this token can control the updater. Keep it secret. Copy Regenerate Running Stopped Error Run on PC to reach this device:
// App list permission hint Only a few apps were detected Only %1$d apps were read. If your device has more installed, the system has not granted this app access to the installed-app list. Allow it in system settings, then pull down to refresh. Open system settings
// Diagnostics grouping GitHub lines F-Droid mirrors Third-party sources %1$d of %2$d usable Fastest: %1$s · %2$d ms No usable line in this group %1$d more hidden (sorted by latency, only the fastest shown)
// Tencent MyApp source Tencent MyApp Queried package by package (the API has no batch mode), limited to 80 apps per scan with concurrency capped at 4.
// Diagnostics optimize button Optimize lines
// Proxy settings Proxy Use custom proxy Route update checks, downloads and icon loading through your proxy. Applied at the HTTP layer, so all sources follow it. Proxy type Choose based on your proxy server HTTP SOCKS Proxy host, e.g. 127.0.0.1 Proxy port Port must be between 1 and 65535
